chapter AFP

session Datalog_Graph = Datalog_Certification +
  description \<open>Datalog-to-graph (Path 2 of the certificate foundedness story). First the purely
    graph-theoretic fact that a finite directed graph has a topological numbering iff it has no
    (directed) cycle (\<open>Graph_Topological_Order\<close>), then the bridge: convert a datalog certificate to
    the graph library's \<open>dgraph\<close> support graph and discharge the foundedness obligation
    \<open>dl_founded\<close> from acyclicity of that graph (\<open>Datalog_To_Graph\<close>). The graph library lives in the
    Base heap, so both build directly on the datalog session.\<close>
  options [timeout = 600]
  theories
    Graph_Topological_Order
    Datalog_To_Graph
